    "title": "No. 4 Kansas City Opens Summit League Play Against Oral Roberts - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Via Kansas City Roos, ,\n1 days ago KANSAS CITY, Mo. – The Kansas City Men’s Soccer team kicks off conference play this weekend as they host Oral Roberts at Durwood Stadium. Kansas City (5-1-2) climbed to No. 4 in this week’s TopDrawerSoccer National Poll following a dramatic week that saw the Roos earn results against two nationally ranked opponents. Kansas City opened the week with a 3-3 draw on the road at then-No. 12 Missouri State last Wednesday. Elouan Labadie-Vincent recorded the first two goals of his Kansas City career, while fifth-year senior Mariano Beunza delivered the equalizer in the 88th minute to secure another result on… Read full article",
